# Redesign: Invoice Management System

## Problem Statement

Invoice creation logic is scattered across 3 separate files, each duplicating the same pattern:

| Current Location | Scenario | Line Items Added |
|---|---|---|
| `BillingsApi.CreateInvoiceAsync` | Initial Subscribe | Subscription + Discount + WalletCredits |
| `SubscriptionRenewalService.CreateInvoiceAsync` | Renewal | Subscription + Overage |
| `PlanSwitchInvoiceFactory.CreatePlanSwitchInvoice` | Plan Switch | Credit + Subscription + Overage (prorated) |

The **pattern is identical** every time: `Create Invoice → Add Line Items → Save`. The only thing that varies is **which line items** get added per scenario.

## Design: Strategy Pattern

We centralize invoice creation into a single **[InvoiceFactory](file:///c:/Users/Mhamed/source/repos/Backend%20Projects/enforcer/backend/src/Modules/Billings/Enforcer.Modules.Billings.Domain/Factories/PlanSwitchInvoiceFactory.cs#10-152)** that accepts a list of **`ILineItemContributor`** strategies. Each contributor knows how to add its specific line items to an invoice.

> [!IMPORTANT]
> The [InvoiceFactory](file:///c:/Users/Mhamed/source/repos/Backend%20Projects/enforcer/backend/src/Modules/Billings/Enforcer.Modules.Billings.Domain/Factories/PlanSwitchInvoiceFactory.cs#10-152) and strategies will live in the **Infrastructure layer** since they depend on external contracts (`PlanResponse`, `SubscriptionResponse`) and services ([PromoCodeService](file:///c:/Users/Mhamed/source/repos/Backend%20Projects/enforcer/backend/src/Modules/Billings/Enforcer.Modules.Billings.Infrastructure/PromotionalCodes/PromoCodeService.cs#9-83)). The pure math ([ProrationCalculatorService](file:///c:/Users/Mhamed/source/repos/Backend%20Projects/enforcer/backend/src/Modules/Billings/Enforcer.Modules.Billings.Infrastructure/Services/ProrationCalculatorService.cs#3-45)) will move to Domain.

```mermaid
graph TD
    A["InvoiceFactory"] --> B["ILineItemContributor"]
    B --> C["SubscriptionLineItemContributor"]
    B --> D["OverageLineItemContributor"]
    B --> E["ProratedSubscriptionContributor"]
    B --> F["CreditForUnusedTimeContributor"]
    B --> G["DiscountLineItemContributor"]
    B --> H["WalletCreditContributor"]
```

### How it works

Each **scenario** (Subscribe, Renew, PlanSwitch) simply picks the right **contributors** and hands them to the factory:

```csharp
// Renewal scenario (inside SubscriptionRenewalService)
var invoice = InvoiceFactory.Create(consumerId, "USD", subscriptionId, periodStart, periodEnd)
    .AddContribution(new SubscriptionContributor(plan))
    .AddContribution(new OverageContributor(plan, apiUsage))
    .Build();

// Plan Switch scenario (inside PlanSwitchBillingService)
var invoice = InvoiceFactory.Create(consumerId, "USD", subscriptionId, now, expiresAt, notes)
    .AddContribution(new CreditForUnusedTimeContributor(currentPlan, expiresAt, now))
    .AddContribution(new ProratedSubscriptionContributor(targetPlan, expiresAt, now))
    .AddContribution(new OverageContributor(currentPlan, apiUsage))
    .Build();
```

